            "body": "## Code Review\n\nThis pull request introduces changes to make the system fully asynchronous. It adds a new run script for `qwen3-235b` and modifies the vLLM rollout utilities for weight updates. My review focuses on a potential typo in the new script that could affect configuration, and a redundant function call in the weight update logic that could impact performance. Addressing these points will improve the correctness and efficiency of the changes.\n\n <sub>**Note:** Security Review did not run due to the size of the PR.</sub>\n\n<details>\n<summary>I am having trouble creating individual review comments. Click here to see my feedback.</summary>\n\n### examples/grpo_trainer/run_qwen3_235b_grpo_npu.sh (141)\n\n![high](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/high-priority.svg)\n\nThere appears to be a typo in this line. The argument starts with `++`, which is not standard Hydra syntax for adding or overriding configurations. This could cause the `use_flash_attn=True` setting to be ignored, potentially impacting performance. It should likely be `+` instead.\n\n```suggestion\n    +actor_rollout_ref.ref.megatron.override_transformer_config.use_flash_attn=True \\\n```\n\n### verl/workers/rollout/vllm_rollout/utils.py (232)\n\n![high](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/high-priority.svg)\n\nThis call to `patch_vllm_moe_model_weight_loader` is redundant. The same function is already called on line 180 before the weight buckets start being received. Since the function is idempotent, calling it again for every bucket within `_update_weights` is unnecessary and can be removed to improve performance during weight synchronization.\n\n</details>",
